      "description": "The ArchiMate subgraph — a NAMED SUBGRAPH of the harness, on the `openapi` subgraph's pattern (owner, 2026-10-09: *\"need new specialixed harness (like openapi) for archimate content in the KG\"*). It holds the machinery for ArchiMate models rather than models: the graph typology `archimate` an instance declares to hold them, the validator for the instance's `cat-archimate.config.json`, the reader for Archi's native format, and the rendering sub-pipeline that gives every view, element and relationship a page and an IRI and draws every view as SVG from the model's own diagram — no Archi install. Of graph typology `cat-harness` because it holds MORE THAN ONE of the harness's parts; the graphs inside it — `archimate-validators` and `archimate-typologies` — are declared FROM WITHIN, in `archimate/graph.json` (#980); its schema and scripts are code, so the tools layer (https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools) holds them (`cat-harness-tools-archimate-schemas`, `cat-harness-tools-archimate`; beans `70lx`, `8lcl`). First instance: smart-ra's DPI-H reference architecture models.",
